  "details": "<p>The Egyptian name Iunet has been attested in the following source, though a primary-source reference for the name has not yet been found: <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://Geissen 2004\" target=\"_self\" title=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/2533/pleiades/items/F7THLSRG/library\">Geissen, Angelo and Manfred Weber, \"Untersuchungen zu den \u00e4gyptischen Nomenpr\u00e4gungen II: 1.-7. Ober\u00e4gyptischer Gau\", <em>Zeitschrift f\u00fcr Papyrologie und Epigraphik</em>, Bd. 147, 2004: pp. 275</a>\u00a0</p>\r\n<div>\u00a0</div>\r\n<div>The Egyptian name Tantere is commonly used and referred to in secondary-source texts, but a primary-source reference has not been found for either.</div>\r\n<div>\u00a0</div>\r\n<div>The name Tentyra can be considered an alternate spelling of Tantura, the primary name used in Greek sources.</div>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Ptolemaic temple to Hathor at Dendera.",
